#. Tag: title
#: dcop.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &k3b; &DCOP; Interface"
msgstr "The &k3b; &DCOP; Interface"

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&k3b; features, like many other &kde; applications as well, a &DCOP; interface "
"which makes it possible to control a part of it's functionality from &eg; a "
"shellscript."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use these &DCOP; functions you can either use the <command>dcop</command> "
"commandline program or the more convenient <application>Kdcop</application> "
"application. Both provide the same functionality so it's mostly a matter of "
"taste and context of usage when deciding which way to choose."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter assumes that you're using the <command>dcop</command> "
"commandline program. To access &k3b;'s &DCOP; functions, make sure that &k3b; "
"is started and then enter something like this at a console:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: dcop.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>#</prompt> <command>dcop</command> <option>k3b</option> <option>"
"K3bInterface</option> <replaceable>[function]</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Besides the generic &DCOP; functions available to all &kde; applications, "
"&k3b;'s DCOP interface mainly consists of two parts as described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: dcop.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default K3bInterface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default K3b DCOP interface provides functionality like copyCD, formatDVD, "
"and methods for creating new projects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: dcop.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"DCOPRef createDataCDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createAudioCDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createMixedCDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createVideoCDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createMovixCDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createDataDVDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createVideoDVDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef createMovixDVDProject()\n"
"DCOPRef openProject(KURL url)\n"
"QValueList&lt;DCOPRef&gt; projects()\n"
"DCOPRef currentProject()\n"
"void copyCd()\n"
"void copyDvd()\n"
"void eraseCdrw()\n"
"void formatDvd()\n"
"void burnCdImage(KURL url)\n"
"void burnDvdImage(KURL url)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As result from one of the createXXXProject methods one gets a DCOP reference to "
"the newly created project: "
"<programlisting>DCOPRef(k3b,K3bProject-0)</programlisting> "
"Alternatively you may create a project using the command line: <screen>\n"
"<prompt>#</prompt> <command>k3b</command> <replaceable>--audiocd</replaceable>\n"
"</screen> and then retrieve a reference to this project with <screen>\n"
"<prompt>#</prompt> <command>dcop</command> <option>k3b</option> <option>"
"K3bInterface</option> <replaceable>currentProject</replaceable>\n"
"</screen> Using this reference it is possible to manipulate the project using "
"the <link linkend=\"k3bprojectinterface\">K3bProjectInterface</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: dcop.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "K3bProjectInterface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: dcop.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"void addUrls(KURL::List urls)\n"
"void addUrl(KURL url)\n"
"void burn()"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"K3b offers the K3bProjectInterface as listed above or the more powerful "
"K3bDataProjectInterface which only applies to data projects (CD and DVD):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: dcop.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"void createFolder(QString name)\n"
"void createFolder(QString name,QString parent)\n"
"void addUrl(KURL url,QString parent)\n"
"void addUrls(KURL::List urls,QString parent)\n"
"void removeItem(QString path)\n"
"void renameItem(QString path,QString newName)\n"
"void setVolumeID(QString id)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: dcop.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this it is possible to fill a data project with files and folders from a "
"script. The following script for example creates a new data project, adds "
"several folders to the project, and adds files to the newly created folders:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: dcop.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
"PROJECT=$(dcop k3b K3bInterface createDataCDProject)\n"
"dcop $PROJECT createFolder test\n"
"dcop $PROJECT createFolder foo\n"
"dcop $PROJECT createFolder bar /foo\n"
"dcop $PROJECT addUrl /home/trueg/somefile.txt /foo/bar"
msgstr ""
